{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794103993,"nonce":"uoBY5yrrlWGXr3Cp24u5jWC5LQE=","title":"Show: the comment box keeps its column when the cursor is on it","message":"## Design\n\n**Aspect changed:** `doc/design/views.md`, \"The comment box\".\n\n- The box always has a one-column gutter on its left, so its text is in the same column whether the cursor is elsewhere, on the box, or typing in it. Today `commentBox.View` (`tui/comment.go`) adds a `›` column only while the cursor is on the box: the text shifts right on arrival and back left on typing.\n- While the cursor is on the box, the gutter's `›` is drawn on the **first line only**; the wash still covers every line, so the box reads as one cell.\n- Not a `›` on every line: a marker repeated down the margin reads as a list, not as one place.\n- It holds wherever the box is drawn, since all three are one `commentBox`: show's comment box, show's description editor, and new's description box.\n\nDesign approved by Luis on 2026-11-07, in a combined review of four stories (box column, side-table arrows, $EDITOR, hints on the bottom line).","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}